{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"Drop push-on-main; add the 6-hourly branch-health schedule, the opt-in gate for the live external tier, and the caller-level main-health-report job."},{"path":".github/workflows/optionality.yml","reason":"Drop push-on-main; add the 6-hourly branch-health schedule."},{"path":".github/workflows/verify-identity.yml","reason":"Drop push-on-main; add the 6-hourly branch-health schedule; refresh the CI-trigger audit comment."},{"path":".github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml","reason":"Drop push-on-main; keep the weekly live-tier cadence unchanged."},{"path":".github/workflows/codeql.yml","reason":"Drop the push-on-main trigger; keep the weekly security-scan schedule; add workflow_dispatch."},{"path":".github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml","reason":"Drop the push-on-main trigger; keep the daily drift sweep."},{"path":"scripts/main_health_report.py","reason":"New: resolves the last-known-green SHA from the Actions API (gh injected as a Runner, the canary_bridge.py pattern) and renders the branch-health run summary — verdict, lower bound, bisect recipe, fail-soft degradation — as a repo script so it is unit-testable."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py","reason":"New regression test pinning the trigger policy: no main-push, preserved non-main push CI, the cadences, dispatch, the report job, and the untouched separate mechanisms."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py","reason":"New test driving the report renderer: green path, red path with a resolved lower bound, and the empty-history degradation path."},{"path":"scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py","reason":"Add the schedule/dispatch-only main-health-report job to EXCLUDED_JOBS (the documented escape hatch) so the Verified-gate parity guard stays green without editing gerrit-verify.yaml."},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","reason":"Record the mirror-CI policy in §3: main CI is scheduled, why, that pre-merge gating is unaffected, and how to respond to a red tick."}]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1785954556015515001,"uuid":"556f250d-b19d-488c-a631-79b49fcbee70"}